Debian/Woody/Alpha users:

Has anyone else running Debian/Woody/Alpha had this problem?
It seems that this morning (after Woody upgrades), many subdirectories under 
/usr have moved to /usr/X11R6 !  For example, /usr/sbin is now none existent 
and at least some of the files that used to exist under there are in 
/usr/X11R6/sbin !  I have noticed the same from /usr/local !  I don't know 
what else has moved.  I am now restoring my backups from amanda.  Thank 
goodness the amanda files (that used to be in /usr/sbin) were in 
/usr/X11R6/sbin or I would not be able to amrestore.  

This is a strange one indeed!  As soon as I figure out the guilty party, he 
gets a huge bug report right before Woody gets released!

